@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Daily Grind
+
+Run `npm start` with Node.js 20 or later. The small Node server listens on
+`PORT` (default `11222`). No dependencies or build step are needed. Deploy behind
+HTTPS and set `PUBLIC_ORIGIN` to the public origin when using a reverse proxy.
+
+Newsletter submissions are posted to `/api/newsletter`. Valid addresses are
+appended to `data/newsletter.jsonl`, or to the directory configured by `DATA_DIR`.
+Use a persistent, private volume in production. This records subscriptions;
+newsletter delivery is a separate process. The server only serves explicitly
+listed homepage assets, so subscription files are never publicly served.
+
+The enforced `Connection-Allowlist` permits only the response origin and
+`https://images.unsplash.com`, retaining default redirect and WebRTC blocking.
+An enforced CSP restricts scripts, styles, fetches, forms, and images as a
+fallback. Connection allowlists have limited browser support; CSP does not
+cover every network channel (such as top-level navigation and WebRTC).
+See the [Connection Allowlists specification](https://wicg.github.io/connection-allowlists/).
+No client-side polyfill can provide equivalent protection in unsupported browsers.
+
+The form supports regular POST submissions without JavaScript. Its enhanced
+flow displays an accessible success or retry message, including for network
+failures, blocked requests, server errors, and a 10-second timeout. Security
+reports are accepted at `/api/security-reports` and discarded without logging
+potentially sensitive report contents.
